1
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:45,360
It's beautiful!
How did you find this restaurant?

2
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:49,720
A colleague in Prague recommended it.
I never got a chance to come before.

3
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:52,280
But after getting the day off yesterday,
I booked a table right away.

4
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:55,000
So you have to thank me for this, right?

5
00:01:56,840 --> 00:01:58,360
Yes, it's all thanks to you.

6
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:04,840
Taking photos again?

7
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:09,800
I'm recording a video.

8
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:12,480
Recording a video?

9
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,960
You seem to really enjoy
taking videos lately.

10
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:16,200
What are you going to use it for?

11
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:18,560
I don't know.

12
00:02:18,640 --> 00:02:20,760
Maybe they'll come in handy someday.

13
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:24,720
Don't tell me you're tired of biology
and want to switch careers?

14
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:30,720
If I ever edit a movie and it's released,
you'd better come see it.

15
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:35,560
We haven't even started drinking
and you're already talking nonsense.

16
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:47,280
You ordered wine?

17
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:50,520
Your colleague recommended this too?

18
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:52,880
When you're in Prague,
you have to try a glass.

19
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:54,600
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

20
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:02,440
It's good.
But I can barely taste the alcohol.

21
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:20,480
Are you still recording?

22
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:23,680
You seem really happy.

23
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:25,880
Of course I am!

24
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:28,720
I've finished presenting my project.
You're almost done with yours too.

25
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:31,120
We're here in Prague,

26
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:35,240
with a beautiful view outside,
and good wine on the table.

27
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:38,240
Sip it slowly.

28
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:39,880
It's fine.

29
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:41,840
I can barely taste the alcohol.
It's like juice.

30
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:46,360
- The kick might sneak up on you later.
- No way!

31
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:59,080
It tastes good!

32
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:04,480
Cheers!

33
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:06,600
This isn't a wine bottle.

34
00:04:08,640 --> 00:04:09,960
This isn't a wine bottle?

35
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:16,000
Then this is a princess's magic wand!

36
00:04:16,079 --> 00:04:20,720
Well, I wonder if I might have the honor
of keeping this magic wand safe for you?

37
00:04:23,880 --> 00:04:25,400
Okay, I'll give it to you.

38
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:27,520
But

39
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:29,440
why are you taking it away?

40
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:32,080
Because you're drunk.

41
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:34,920
No, I'm not. Not at all.

42
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:37,760
How are you not?

43
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:39,800
The last time you got drunk,
you acted just like this.

44
00:04:41,080 --> 00:04:44,240
But you're actually pretty cute
when you drink too much. Like a kitten.

45
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:47,760
A kitten? What does a kitten look like?

46
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:52,640
Let me record it and show you.
Then you'll see.

47
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:58,000
This is so hard.

48
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:02,040
What question could possibly
stump our Ms. Zheng?

49
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:03,520
I…

50
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:07,520
Before I came here,
I had so many things planned to tell you.

51
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:08,960
Fangli even gave me advice

52
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:10,560
on how to say sweet things

53
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:12,080
and act cute.

54
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:16,880
But ever since I got here,
I haven't said a single word of it.

55
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:25,200
Aren't you pretty good at acting cute?
Remember Qingshan Island?

56
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:28,240
Qingshan Island?

57
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:30,960
Chen Yanzhou.

58
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:34,680
I know you were just
playing along back then.

59
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:40,120
Forget it. If I don't know it, so be it.

60
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:42,480
Exactly. If you don't know it, so be it.

61
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:44,360
You don't have to be good at everything.

62
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:46,280
That's right.
As long as you can do it.

63
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:52,000
I want to hear you act cute.

64
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:54,200
You… You're the best at it.

65
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:55,920
Can you do it for me to hear, please?

66
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:02,440
Okay.

67
00:06:02,520 --> 00:06:03,720
What kind do you want to hear?

68
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:07,320
Let's start with something simple.

69
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,480
Like "kitty" or "puppy."

70
00:06:09,560 --> 00:06:12,040
Just cute words like that.

71
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:15,600
Okay.

72
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:20,560
I want

73
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:21,680
a hug.

74
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:27,440
I want

75
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:28,920
a kiss.

76
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:31,760
How was that?

77
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:32,840
Did I pass?

78
00:06:35,680 --> 00:06:36,880
I want a hug!

79
00:06:36,960 --> 00:06:38,640
I want

80
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:39,560
a kiss.

81
00:06:44,640 --> 00:06:46,840
Our Ms. Zheng is still a quick learner.

82
00:07:01,320 --> 00:07:02,640
Chen Yanzhou.

83
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:06,600
Besides hugs and kisses,
I want to sway too.

84
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:09,040
Sway?

85
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:10,760
It's like

86
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:12,160
this, and this.

87
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:13,480
And then…

88
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:16,480
And then like this,

89
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:17,760
and this.

90
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:19,560
You want to dance?

91
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:23,320
How do you want to dance?

92
00:07:25,440 --> 00:07:26,880
You haven't even asked me.

93
00:07:31,920 --> 00:07:33,320
So half-hearted.

94
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:41,880
My princess,

95
00:07:41,960 --> 00:07:43,960
may I have this dance with you?

96
00:08:14,760 --> 00:08:16,080
Chen Yanzhou.

97
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:18,680
Did I just step on your foot?

98
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:21,120
That's the seventh time.

99
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:23,440
Then why didn't you dodge?

100
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:26,080
I didn't want to.

101
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:28,920
Having the princess
step on my feet is an honor.

102
00:08:57,200 --> 00:08:58,120
How is it?

103
00:08:58,840 --> 00:09:00,680
Feeling a little more sober
after swaying around?

104
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:03,120
I was completely sober to begin with!

105
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:10,720
Chen Yanzhou.

106
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:12,480
You're so handsome.

107
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:17,360
My boyfriend is really handsome.

108
00:09:19,040 --> 00:09:20,600
Looks like you're still not fully sober.

109
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:23,520
You only say things like this
when you're drunk.

110
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:26,720
Then from now on, I'll tell you every day.

111
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:31,000
Say it more. I love hearing it.

112
00:09:36,640 --> 00:09:37,920
It's so beautiful here.

113
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:40,440
But Qingyi is even more beautiful.

114
00:09:43,240 --> 00:09:44,600
Chen Yanzhou.

115
00:09:45,160 --> 00:09:47,080
I'm feeling a little homesick.

116
00:09:56,800 --> 00:09:58,760
Then let's go back and visit.

117
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:06,000
HI, HAVE A NICE TRIP!
BERLIN - QINGYI

118
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:07,200
Chen Yanzhou.

119
00:10:07,280 --> 00:10:08,760
You…

120
00:10:08,840 --> 00:10:10,080
Are you a magician?

121
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:12,320
No, I'm not.

122
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:16,520
Maybe it's because
I have the princess's magic wand.

123
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:20,040
You're treating me like a three-year-old.

124
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:26,400
A while ago, I noticed you kept
looking at your chat with Xiaomian.

125
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:28,880
I was feeling homesick too,
so I bought two tickets.

126
00:10:54,920 --> 00:10:56,880
Here, let's have a drink.

127
00:10:56,960 --> 00:10:57,880
Cheers.

128
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:11,400
In the old days,
when you two walked together,

129
00:11:11,480 --> 00:11:13,200
there was still room for me between you.

130
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:15,880
But now, you two barely leave room
for a sheet of paper!

131
00:11:17,400 --> 00:11:20,320
Really? I seem to remember you were
always squeezing between us.

132
00:11:20,400 --> 00:11:22,520
Am I really the kind of person

133
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:24,560
who's that tactless and oblivious?

134
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:28,720
Didn't someone try to play matchmaker
for the wrong people before?

135
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:30,560
What do you mean by playing matchmaker?

136
00:11:30,640 --> 00:11:34,360
Let's not bring up the past.
I'll drink to make up for it.

137
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:37,560
I'll tell you about it later.

138
00:11:39,160 --> 00:11:41,840
Hey, keep public decorum in mind.
There is still a person right here.

139
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:46,480
Do you two know

140
00:11:47,160 --> 00:11:50,160
that when I saw
Zheng Yu's post on Moments,

141
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:52,480
I was right in the middle of
doing a Western blot?

142
00:11:52,560 --> 00:11:54,440
I know. You mentioned that ages ago.

143
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:57,480
What I didn't mention was that
I was cutting the membrane at the time.

144
00:11:58,160 --> 00:12:01,400
When I saw the post, my hand slipped
and I cut off the internal control.

145
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:03,520
The entire batch of samples was ruined!

146
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:06,080
That's a problem
with your lab skills then.

147
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:07,880
Exactly, and you're blaming us for that?

148
00:12:09,680 --> 00:12:11,760
Fine. You two are on the same team now.

149
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:13,400
I'm not arguing with you.

150
00:12:15,760 --> 00:12:17,480
How long are you staying this time?

151
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:19,240
Not long. We're leaving in two days.

152
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:21,320
Leaving so soon?

153
00:12:21,920 --> 00:12:23,400
Try studying in Germany sometime.

154
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:24,920
Me? I'd never put myself through that.

155
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:29,080
Then where are you staying
while you're here?

156
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:31,920
I know Chen Yanzhou's place
is near Qing Yi University,

157
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,440
but you're not from Qingyi.

158
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:36,160
Or are you going back
to your hometown for a few days?

159
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:39,840
Bi Dezheng.

160
00:12:39,920 --> 00:12:42,320
Guess where we set off from
to come have dinner here?

161
00:12:42,400 --> 00:12:43,800
How would I know?

162
00:12:43,880 --> 00:12:46,320
If we had that kind of telepathy,
Zheng Yu would be jealous.

163
00:12:48,240 --> 00:12:49,120
My family's house.

164
00:12:51,160 --> 00:12:52,520
You already met his parents?

165
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:57,240
They've met before.

166
00:13:00,800 --> 00:13:02,120
"They've met before."

167
00:13:04,280 --> 00:13:05,560
Okay, it's my bad.

168
00:13:05,640 --> 00:13:07,160
I'll drink to make up for it, okay?

169
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:16,160
Zheng Yu.

170
00:13:16,240 --> 00:13:17,080
Listen.

171
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:19,440
If Chen Yanzhou ever picks on you,

172
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:21,160
tell me.

173
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:22,960
I may not be able to beat him,

174
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:24,120
but I can…

175
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:25,840
You can what?

176
00:13:27,960 --> 00:13:29,080
I can cry to him.

177
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:34,880
Chen Yanzhou, you too.

178
00:13:34,960 --> 00:13:36,120
If Zheng Yu ever picks on you…

179
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:39,080
What will you do?

180
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:42,040
I… I'd advise you to bear it.

181
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:47,200
Bi Dezheng, you're really good
at applying rules flexibly.

182
00:13:47,280 --> 00:13:48,320
Of course.

183
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:52,360
Being able to see you two so happy…

184
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:56,720
makes me happy too.

185
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:27,320
Good thing I still remembered
where Bi Dezheng's graduate dorm was.

186
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:29,600
Otherwise, we'd have had to take him home.

187
00:14:29,680 --> 00:14:31,040
I wouldn't have minded.

188
00:14:31,840 --> 00:14:32,840
I would have.

189
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:39,960
What's so funny?

190
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,080
Come to think of it,

191
00:14:42,160 --> 00:14:44,760
I've walked down this road
countless times before.

192
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:46,160
But I never imagined

193
00:14:46,240 --> 00:14:48,800
that walking down it while
holding your hand would feel so different.

194
00:14:50,040 --> 00:14:51,240
Did you ever imagine it?

195
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:53,400
Imagine what?

196
00:14:54,400 --> 00:14:57,760
Back at that first meeting,
did you ever imagine that someday,

197
00:14:57,840 --> 00:15:01,800
you would share so many experiences
and have such a journey together?

198
00:15:02,800 --> 00:15:05,240
Oh? That first meeting with who?

199
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:07,960
Who do you think?

200
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:16,920
To be honest, no.

201
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:19,480
After all, back then,
a certain someone suddenly showed up

202
00:15:19,560 --> 00:15:21,840
and took away the scholarship
I needed to pay off my debt.

203
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:24,600
Why would I want to have
anything to do with that person?

204
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:27,560
And what about later on?

205
00:15:30,160 --> 00:15:31,320
Later…

206
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:34,400
Later, you told me that you wanted
to win together with me,

207
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:36,280
and that we were friends.

208
00:15:36,880 --> 00:15:40,280
Gradually, I realized you
weren't quite what I had imagined.

209
00:15:42,680 --> 00:15:43,920
How was I different?

210
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:46,640
At first, I found it strange.

211
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:51,320
You were cold and distant at school,
but when I went to your house,

212
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:53,600
I saw how cheerful you were
around your family.

213
00:15:53,680 --> 00:15:58,080
It took a long time for me
to understand that behind that smile,

214
00:15:58,160 --> 00:15:59,280
there were so many stories.

215
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:03,040
After going through
so much together,

216
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:06,600
I feel like I can
truly be myself around you.

217
00:16:07,640 --> 00:16:09,320
And that made me realize

218
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:11,880
that I wanted to share a story
with someone like you.

219
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:16,280
What about you?

220
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:18,000
When we first met,

221
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:20,360
did you already guess
we'd go through so much together?

222
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:24,800
I didn't know.

223
00:16:25,760 --> 00:16:27,000
But…

224
00:16:28,240 --> 00:16:29,080
I had a hunch.

225
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:32,080
Because back then, I was just
so curious about you.

226
00:16:32,760 --> 00:16:35,680
How could someone ask me
to hit them with a ball

227
00:16:35,760 --> 00:16:38,360
just to cover up the fact that
they were subbing for a class?

228
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:40,560
And as if running the 1500
wasn't enough,

229
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:42,000
you went and ran
the 3,000 m too!

230
00:16:42,680 --> 00:16:45,200
Speaking of the scholarship,
I also wondered

231
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:46,920
why someone who needed
that money so badly

232
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:49,080
would still clear my name
when I was accused of cheating.

233
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:53,720
Isn't curiosity supposed to be
the prelude to falling in love?

234
00:16:55,520 --> 00:16:59,000
I used to think this city
was just a place to exist in.

235
00:16:59,080 --> 00:17:02,240
Every day, I'd go to class,
then come home, eat, and sleep.

236
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:03,760
It was always the same.

237
00:17:04,920 --> 00:17:07,960
But eventually, I started seeing it
as a city full of possibilities.

238
00:17:09,119 --> 00:17:11,400
Because whenever
I walked down the street,

239
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:13,240
I might run into you
at any moment.

240
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:17,760
I never knew you had
so many thoughts

241
00:17:17,839 --> 00:17:19,760
running through
your head back then.

242
00:17:20,920 --> 00:17:21,960
Of course.

243
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:34,480
It's our dorm group chat.

244
00:17:36,320 --> 00:17:38,320
You girls seem to chat pretty often.

245
00:17:39,440 --> 00:17:42,120
Especially since I just got back.
We plan to meet up.

246
00:17:49,440 --> 00:17:51,040
Why aren't you saying anything?

247
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:54,000
I was wondering

248
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:58,160
if you ever talk to other people about us
the way you just did then.

249
00:17:59,280 --> 00:18:00,720
Not really.

250
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:02,720
But sometimes,
you do come up in conversation.

251
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:05,240
I tell them…

252
00:18:05,320 --> 00:18:06,160
You tell them what?

253
00:18:09,120 --> 00:18:11,880
What else would you discuss with friends
when talking about boyfriends?

254
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:13,920
Of course

255
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,120
I tell them about your flaws.

256
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:19,840
Then tell me, what flaws do I have?

257
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:24,480
You…

258
00:18:24,560 --> 00:18:25,680
get jealous easily.

259
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:28,440
And…

260
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:33,960
Is it really that hard?

261
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:37,120
How about I list them myself then?

262
00:18:37,920 --> 00:18:38,920
Jealous.

263
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:41,560
Petty.

264
00:18:42,720 --> 00:18:43,800
Childish.

265
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:46,240
Clingy.

266
00:18:49,480 --> 00:18:51,640
Chen Yanzhou,
what are you doing?

267
00:18:53,640 --> 00:18:55,800
Offering my formal apologies
for all my flaws.

268
00:18:56,800 --> 00:18:57,800
All you do is sweet-talk me.

269
00:18:59,040 --> 00:19:01,240
Fine. Let's add that
to the list.

270
00:19:07,600 --> 00:19:09,120
Chen Yanzhou!

271
00:19:09,200 --> 00:19:10,960
Are you planning
to spend the whole night

272
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:12,120
listing all your flaws?

273
00:19:12,920 --> 00:19:15,560
I wouldn't mind. We've got
all the time in the world.

274
00:19:17,160 --> 00:19:19,200
You're just looking
for an excuse to kiss me.

275
00:19:22,280 --> 00:19:23,520
You caught me!

276
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:28,080
Chen Yanzhou, you're getting
more shameless by the day.

277
00:19:30,160 --> 00:19:31,760
Well, count that
as another flaw then.

278
00:19:41,320 --> 00:19:43,200
That's enough. Let's go home.

279
00:19:54,720 --> 00:19:57,120
By the way, when are you
meeting your roommates?

280
00:19:58,280 --> 00:19:59,280
Tomorrow.

281
00:20:00,040 --> 00:20:01,920
Okay, I'll pick you up
afterward.

282
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:14,000
So you can speak German now?

283
00:20:15,120 --> 00:20:16,600
I can handle basic conversations.

284
00:20:16,680 --> 00:20:19,680
I've also learned some technical terms,
so I can follow lectures more easily.

285
00:20:20,280 --> 00:20:22,080
That's amazing, Zheng Yu!

286
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:25,400
"The sun is super intense today
and I'm practically melting."

287
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:27,920
- How do you say that in German?
- Come on!

288
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:31,240
I just got back home and you're already
making me keep studying German?

289
00:20:31,320 --> 00:20:32,720
Okay, fine.

290
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:35,360
I'll ask something easier
than German then.

291
00:20:36,080 --> 00:20:37,360
A relationship question!

292
00:20:37,440 --> 00:20:40,240
How far have things gotten
between you and Chen Yanzhou?

293
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:44,080
I think I'll answer
your previous question instead.

294
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:45,800
Which German phrase did you want to know?

295
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:46,760
Okay, okay.

296
00:20:46,840 --> 00:20:48,600
You don't have to answer.
We get the picture.

297
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:52,080
You all already know that German phrase?

298
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:54,120
Well, let me hear you say it then.

299
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:56,400
I'll see which of you
has the better pronunciation.

300
00:20:56,920 --> 00:20:58,160
Now you've learned to play dumb!

301
00:20:58,240 --> 00:21:00,680
What were we talking about
over dinner earlier?

302
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:03,640
Was it Zhuang Ning's
showdown with her boss

303
00:21:03,720 --> 00:21:06,240
or Linlin's new crush?

304
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:09,280
I think we were talking about
you meeting Song Mo's parents!

305
00:21:10,040 --> 00:21:13,280
Look at her! On top of playing dumb,
she's learned how to shift the spotlight!

306
00:21:13,360 --> 00:21:14,880
Fine, I won't say anything then.

307
00:21:17,960 --> 00:21:19,480
Is Chen Yanzhou coming to pick you up?

308
00:21:20,560 --> 00:21:22,600
We need to pick up his cousin
and my brother in a bit.

309
00:21:22,680 --> 00:21:23,960
They went out together.

310
00:21:24,040 --> 00:21:26,640
Well, look at you!
You've got everything all planned out.

311
00:21:26,720 --> 00:21:29,720
- You're already taking the kids along!
- Xu Fangli! You…

312
00:21:31,560 --> 00:21:34,560
Seriously though, Zheng Yu,
you really have changed a lot.

313
00:21:34,640 --> 00:21:35,640
Really?

314
00:21:35,720 --> 00:21:36,800
You smile so much more now!

315
00:21:36,880 --> 00:21:40,240
Do you realize how low your threshold
for laughing is these days?

316
00:21:40,320 --> 00:21:41,640
Just like right now!

317
00:21:41,720 --> 00:21:43,760
- I'll take a photo so she can see!
- Snap a photo of her!

318
00:21:45,920 --> 00:21:47,200
- Look at this.
- Let me see.

319
00:21:49,840 --> 00:21:50,840
Right?

320
00:21:52,120 --> 00:21:53,360
We're at the entrance.

321
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:56,080
Here!

322
00:22:09,200 --> 00:22:12,000
Whose boyfriend is this?

323
00:22:13,440 --> 00:22:14,520
Hers.

324
00:22:17,280 --> 00:22:19,480
Come on, we were not actually asking.

325
00:22:20,440 --> 00:22:22,920
You're here to pick her up so early.
We've barely finished eating.

326
00:22:24,040 --> 00:22:25,440
My bad. It's my mistake.

327
00:22:27,360 --> 00:22:30,400
Since you and Zheng Yu brought us gifts,
we'll let you off the hook.

328
00:22:30,480 --> 00:22:32,400
Thanks for the gifts!

329
00:22:32,920 --> 00:22:35,800
As for us, we wouldn't mind
if you came back more often.

330
00:22:35,880 --> 00:22:38,480
Got it. Well, we have plans,
so we should keep moving.

331
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:41,760
- Bye.
- Bye.

332
00:22:41,840 --> 00:22:43,560
Let's keep in touch on WeChat!

333
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:46,720
What a gentleman!

334
00:22:49,280 --> 00:22:51,720
- Bye!
- Bye!

335
00:22:51,800 --> 00:22:53,160
Don't miss me too much!

336
00:22:53,240 --> 00:22:55,120
- We'll miss you!
- We'll miss you!

337
00:22:55,720 --> 00:22:57,960
- Bye!
- Take care!

338
00:23:02,680 --> 00:23:04,320
Tell me.

339
00:23:04,400 --> 00:23:07,000
Can love really change a person this much?

340
00:23:08,280 --> 00:23:09,480
What if it's not changing her,

341
00:23:09,560 --> 00:23:12,040
but rather restoring her
to the person she originally was?

342
00:23:12,960 --> 00:23:15,640
Xiaozhuang Ning,
that was surprisingly deep!

343
00:23:20,240 --> 00:23:23,080
Song Mo is almost here.
I'd better get going too.

344
00:23:23,160 --> 00:23:24,840
Let's catch up another time, bye!

345
00:23:24,920 --> 00:23:27,440
You were just lecturing Zheng Yu,
and now you're the first to run off!

346
00:23:27,520 --> 00:23:28,520
Just go already!

347
00:23:28,600 --> 00:23:31,040
- Bye.
- Bye.

348
00:23:31,120 --> 00:23:32,520
Aren't you used to it by now?

349
00:23:33,600 --> 00:23:34,440
Let's go.

350
00:23:35,040 --> 00:23:37,240
When will love finally come my way?

351
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:40,880
I heard Germany is famous for its beer.

352
00:23:40,960 --> 00:23:42,360
Has your drinking improved?

353
00:23:43,080 --> 00:23:44,480
I don't drink much.

354
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:48,160
That's true. What's so great
about beer anyway?

355
00:23:50,400 --> 00:23:52,280
Are there lots of
handsome guys in Germany?

356
00:23:53,600 --> 00:23:56,040
Tell me secretly.
I promise I won't tell Yanzhou.

357
00:23:56,120 --> 00:23:57,040
Well…

358
00:23:57,120 --> 00:23:59,640
Gao Xing. I can hear you.

359
00:23:59,720 --> 00:24:02,160
Cover your ears. Then you won't hear!

360
00:24:03,240 --> 00:24:05,120
Are there lots of them?

361
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:07,520
- Is it--
- Didn't your phone just ring?

362
00:24:07,600 --> 00:24:08,840
Was that your mom calling?

363
00:24:08,920 --> 00:24:11,200
What if it's something big,
like college preferences?

364
00:24:11,280 --> 00:24:14,520
You must be hearing things!
My phone's on silent.

365
00:24:14,600 --> 00:24:16,720
Besides, I've already
submitted my applications.

366
00:24:17,760 --> 00:24:19,800
Really? What did you put
as your first choice?

367
00:24:22,840 --> 00:24:24,040
It's a secret.

368
00:24:27,920 --> 00:24:29,480
Xiaomian, how's university life?

369
00:24:30,600 --> 00:24:31,440
It's pretty good.

370
00:24:32,560 --> 00:24:34,720
The computer science program
at Ji An University is great.

371
00:24:34,800 --> 00:24:38,800
I heard you wrote some kind of program
and even sold it recently.

372
00:24:39,960 --> 00:24:42,480
It was a pretty simple program.
I didn't make much from it.

373
00:24:42,560 --> 00:24:45,080
That's still impressive.
Gao Xing keeps telling me about it.

374
00:24:46,560 --> 00:24:48,040
Gao Xing did pretty well on her exams.

375
00:24:48,120 --> 00:24:49,800
You deserve credit for tutoring her.

376
00:24:50,840 --> 00:24:53,280
She must've been a handful.
You worked hard.

377
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:56,080
Yanzhou. I can hear you.

378
00:24:57,360 --> 00:24:59,040
Cover your ears. Then you won't hear.

379
00:25:02,280 --> 00:25:04,680
How much longer until we reach the beach?

380
00:25:04,760 --> 00:25:06,200
I can't take this driver anymore.

381
00:25:06,960 --> 00:25:08,240
Watch what you say.

382
00:25:08,320 --> 00:25:10,360
Your cousin might dump you
on the side of the road.

383
00:25:12,880 --> 00:25:15,520
Now he can't.

384
00:25:21,680 --> 00:25:24,680
Yanzhou, you're so unoriginal.

385
00:25:25,440 --> 00:25:28,400
Next time, can you take us somewhere new?
We've already been here.

386
00:25:29,440 --> 00:25:30,680
I think it's nice here.

387
00:25:31,320 --> 00:25:33,200
Actually, now I look again,

388
00:25:33,280 --> 00:25:35,800
different seasons
really do have different vibes.

389
00:25:35,880 --> 00:25:37,720
I take back what I just said.

390
00:25:38,760 --> 00:25:40,160
You change your mind so quickly.

391
00:25:42,680 --> 00:25:45,000
Gao Xing, what's that thing
hanging on your bag?

392
00:25:45,600 --> 00:25:48,760
A good luck charm. It's a popular way
to wish good fortune online.

393
00:25:48,840 --> 00:25:49,920
It's really trendy.

394
00:25:50,640 --> 00:25:52,240
Xiaomian, you know quite a lot.

395
00:25:53,920 --> 00:25:55,880
I just happened to
hear about it from someone.

396
00:25:56,840 --> 00:25:58,080
Did you make it yourself?

397
00:25:58,880 --> 00:26:00,120
Of course not.

398
00:26:00,720 --> 00:26:02,800
It won't work if you make it yourself.

399
00:26:02,880 --> 00:26:06,120
- It only works if someone gives it to you.
- Someone?

400
00:26:06,200 --> 00:26:07,320
Who is this "someone"?

401
00:26:09,240 --> 00:26:11,680
Isn't that the spot
where we took photos last time?

402
00:26:11,760 --> 00:26:13,160
Let's take another one there.

403
00:26:13,920 --> 00:26:15,600
What do you think,

404
00:26:15,680 --> 00:26:17,160
cousin-in-law?

405
00:26:17,240 --> 00:26:18,640
In-law…

406
00:26:18,720 --> 00:26:21,920
When you guys came to the beach last time,
you didn't bring me along.

407
00:26:22,000 --> 00:26:23,440
I want to take photos this time too.

408
00:26:23,520 --> 00:26:24,880
Is it okay, brother-in-law?

409
00:26:25,720 --> 00:26:26,880
In-law…

410
00:26:30,280 --> 00:26:31,880
Yes, of course we'll take photos!

411
00:26:31,960 --> 00:26:33,960
Gao Xing, where's the camera?
Hurry and take it out.

412
00:26:34,040 --> 00:26:35,560
- Come on, let's take yours first.
- Okay!

413
00:26:35,640 --> 00:26:36,840
I'll go with him.

414
00:26:38,480 --> 00:26:40,520
Yanzhou, I'll take photos
of you two in a bit!

415
00:26:42,880 --> 00:26:44,600
Fine then. Strike a pose!

416
00:26:46,600 --> 00:26:48,600
You're so far apart.
How is that a couple photo?

417
00:26:49,680 --> 00:26:50,760
Move closer.

418
00:26:52,560 --> 00:26:53,880
A little closer.

419
00:26:59,480 --> 00:27:01,720
Three, two, one.

420
00:27:02,760 --> 00:27:04,240
All right.

421
00:27:04,320 --> 00:27:06,680
All right, let me take photos of you two!

422
00:27:17,680 --> 00:27:20,200
Ms. Zheng, you've changed.

423
00:27:20,880 --> 00:27:23,720
You weren't like this last time.
You were practically out of the frame!

424
00:27:26,080 --> 00:27:29,000
That's because back then,
I wasn't that close to your cousin.

425
00:27:29,680 --> 00:27:32,080
Watch your wording. We were only
not close from your perspective.

426
00:27:32,920 --> 00:27:34,480
Not true.

427
00:27:34,560 --> 00:27:37,000
- Do you want me to explain in detail?
- Go ahead then.

428
00:27:37,080 --> 00:27:38,800
- So you want me to spell it out?
- Do it.

429
00:27:38,880 --> 00:27:40,680
Okay, stop bickering!

430
00:27:40,760 --> 00:27:43,440
Let's take a photo first.
Are you ready?

431
00:27:44,800 --> 00:27:45,680
Three,

432
00:27:46,520 --> 00:27:47,520
two,

433
00:27:48,200 --> 00:27:49,200
one.

434
00:28:04,680 --> 00:28:06,840
Weren't you two just bickering
a second ago?

435
00:28:06,920 --> 00:28:09,480
How did that turn into…?

436
00:28:11,400 --> 00:28:13,640
It's called romance.
You wouldn't understand.

437
00:28:14,240 --> 00:28:16,640
Romance my foot!
That's not suitable for kids!

438
00:28:17,640 --> 00:28:18,560
Let me see the photo.

439
00:28:18,640 --> 00:28:20,320
- No!
- Just one look!

440
00:28:20,400 --> 00:28:21,920
- No way!
- Gao Xing!

441
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:23,840
- Let me look at the photo!
- No way!

442
00:28:23,920 --> 00:28:25,320
- Let me see it!
- No way!

443
00:28:26,720 --> 00:28:28,320
Hey, stop running!
Name your price.

444
00:28:29,600 --> 00:28:30,440
Twenty thousand.

445
00:28:31,400 --> 00:28:32,440
Deal.

446
00:28:33,600 --> 00:28:35,680
I've changed my mind.
Fifty thousand.

447
00:28:35,760 --> 00:28:36,760
Transfer it now.

448
00:28:38,280 --> 00:28:39,120
Deal.

449
00:28:39,880 --> 00:28:41,760
That's too much.
We can just retake it.

450
00:28:41,840 --> 00:28:42,960
I'll sell it to you.

451
00:28:43,040 --> 00:28:43,960
At a discount even!

452
00:28:45,320 --> 00:28:46,640
Ms. Zheng!

453
00:28:46,720 --> 00:28:48,800
You're messing up the market
and playing dirty.

454
00:28:52,160 --> 00:28:54,120
You two, slow down. Don't fall.

455
00:28:54,720 --> 00:28:56,400
Jiang Mian, whose side are you on?

456
00:28:57,880 --> 00:28:59,200
I…

457
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:00,880
I'm not taking sides.

458
00:29:00,960 --> 00:29:02,360
Then we're no longer friends!

459
00:29:03,040 --> 00:29:05,120
Zheng Yu, slow down!
Gao Xing, stop messing around!

460
00:29:25,080 --> 00:29:27,280
Are you guys heading back
to Berlin already?

461
00:29:27,360 --> 00:29:28,920
Why? Are you going to miss us?

462
00:29:29,440 --> 00:29:30,720
Not at all!

463
00:29:31,680 --> 00:29:33,560
Okay, maybe a little.

464
00:29:34,280 --> 00:29:37,320
Whenever you guys have free time,
come visit us in Germany.

465
00:29:37,400 --> 00:29:39,880
- I'm free tomorrow!
- Gao Xing!

466
00:29:39,960 --> 00:29:42,160
- You can't go tomorrow.
- Why not?

467
00:29:42,240 --> 00:29:43,640
You don't even have a visa yet.

468
00:29:45,480 --> 00:29:47,080
You're such a buzzkill!

469
00:29:47,800 --> 00:29:49,240
Xiaomian's just
looking out for you.

470
00:29:49,320 --> 00:29:52,240
Yanzhou, you always
side with outsiders!

471
00:29:53,960 --> 00:29:56,040
It's not like
he's ever sided with you.

472
00:29:57,400 --> 00:29:59,520
Try saying that
one more time!

473
00:30:00,920 --> 00:30:02,640
Gao Xing, don't get physical!

474
00:30:06,160 --> 00:30:07,720
Can I get physical then?

475
00:30:27,680 --> 00:30:31,600
ONE YEAR LATER

476
00:30:32,840 --> 00:30:33,720
Hello, good morning!

477
00:30:33,800 --> 00:30:35,680
It is currently 7:15 a.m.

478
00:30:35,760 --> 00:30:38,560
Today is the day of
Ms. Zheng's sharing session.

479
00:30:38,640 --> 00:30:41,080
Let's see what color outfit
Ms. Zheng chooses to wear today!

480
00:30:45,480 --> 00:30:46,760
She is carefully

481
00:30:46,840 --> 00:30:48,960
inspecting her wardrobe
to see what colors she has.

482
00:30:49,560 --> 00:30:51,240
Ms. Zheng has chosen

483
00:30:51,320 --> 00:30:53,240
a beige-colored outfit.

484
00:30:54,800 --> 00:30:56,240
It's creamy yellow.

485
00:30:57,640 --> 00:30:59,040
Creamy yellow.

486
00:31:01,640 --> 00:31:02,800
Is there a difference?

487
00:31:02,880 --> 00:31:04,880
Ms. Zheng
has picked up a belt,

488
00:31:04,960 --> 00:31:07,520
which is great for
breaking up the monotony

489
00:31:07,600 --> 00:31:10,160
and adding a nice
finishing touch.

490
00:31:11,080 --> 00:31:12,760
Now she's wrapped it
around her neck.

491
00:31:12,840 --> 00:31:15,960
That is, presumably,
probably, a silk scarf.

492
00:31:16,040 --> 00:31:18,640
Okay, Ms. Zheng has
taken it off again.

493
00:31:18,720 --> 00:31:20,440
Let's see
what she'll do next--

494
00:31:20,520 --> 00:31:22,000
Ms. Zheng is resorting
to violence!

495
00:31:22,080 --> 00:31:24,080
I messed up the commentary,
but does it warrant this?

496
00:31:24,160 --> 00:31:25,240
I'm going to get changed!

497
00:31:28,480 --> 00:31:31,880
Well then, let's all look forward
to Ms. Zheng's final outfit choice today!

498
00:31:31,960 --> 00:31:33,040
Bye!

499
00:31:34,040 --> 00:31:37,600
Ms. Zheng is now sitting across
from me, getting ready to eat.

500
00:31:37,680 --> 00:31:41,480
Let's see what Ms. Zheng is having
for breakfast before her sharing session!

501
00:31:43,440 --> 00:31:44,760
This is way too lavish!

502
00:31:44,840 --> 00:31:46,400
Who prepared all this?

503
00:31:46,480 --> 00:31:48,400
Turns out Chef Xiaozhou made it!

504
00:31:48,480 --> 00:31:50,400
Why are you giving yourself
extra screen time?

505
00:31:51,080 --> 00:31:52,520
Am I?

506
00:31:54,720 --> 00:31:55,760
Hi!

507
00:31:57,440 --> 00:31:58,320
Hurry up and eat.

508
00:31:58,400 --> 00:32:00,560
Don't you still have to
escort me to the venue later?

509
00:32:04,600 --> 00:32:05,440
As you wish.

510
00:32:05,520 --> 00:32:08,000
Ms. Zheng's safety is in the hands
of Bodyguard Xiaozhou.

511
00:32:10,000 --> 00:32:12,160
It is currently 8:20 a.m.

512
00:32:12,960 --> 00:32:14,520
Ms. Zheng is now taking the subway

513
00:32:14,600 --> 00:32:16,040
to the sharing session.

514
00:32:16,920 --> 00:32:19,600
She likely needs some time
to do mental preparation.

515
00:32:20,280 --> 00:32:22,640
Says who? I do not!

516
00:32:23,400 --> 00:32:27,560
But someone has already read her speech
three times since leaving home

517
00:32:27,640 --> 00:32:29,880
and checked her USB drive twice.

518
00:32:31,440 --> 00:32:32,400
Chen Yanzhou.

519
00:32:35,720 --> 00:32:36,800
That last part?

520
00:32:37,920 --> 00:32:38,760
Delete it.

521
00:32:50,640 --> 00:32:53,200
Now we have arrived
at the entrance of the sharing session.

522
00:32:55,080 --> 00:32:56,440
Well, I'm heading in.

523
00:32:58,240 --> 00:32:59,760
I'll wait for you outside.

524
00:32:59,840 --> 00:33:00,920
Good luck!

525
00:33:21,440 --> 00:33:23,000
Why am I stuck outside?

526
00:33:23,080 --> 00:33:25,480
Because I'm not a student here.

527
00:33:30,280 --> 00:33:32,560
Honestly, isn't this rule
a little unreasonable?

528
00:33:32,640 --> 00:33:34,360
They should make an exception for family.

529
00:33:36,960 --> 00:33:38,600
I just went to buy flowers.

530
00:33:43,080 --> 00:33:43,960
There's a poster of

531
00:33:44,040 --> 00:33:45,480
Ms. Zheng's sharing session.

532
00:33:46,240 --> 00:33:48,120
And here's her name.

533
00:33:49,320 --> 00:33:51,560
Our Ms. Zheng really is quite photogenic!

534
00:33:52,640 --> 00:33:55,880
Now, I'll give everyone a tour
of Ms. Zheng's university.

535
00:33:56,800 --> 00:33:58,960
This is their exhibition hall.

536
00:33:59,040 --> 00:34:00,920
And that's their sports field.

537
00:34:01,000 --> 00:34:04,280
This is where I just saw Ms. Zheng's
sharing session poster just now.

538
00:34:05,360 --> 00:34:06,920
And this is her classroom.

539
00:34:07,840 --> 00:34:09,159
She should be coming out soon.

540
00:34:09,239 --> 00:34:10,760
AUDITORIUM 2

541
00:34:14,440 --> 00:34:15,639
As expected.

542
00:35:46,640 --> 00:35:47,640
Let's go home.

543
00:35:50,320 --> 00:35:51,160
Wait.

544
00:35:52,440 --> 00:35:53,360
I need one last shot.

545
00:35:57,520 --> 00:35:59,520
I'm heading home with our Ms. Zheng.

546
00:36:01,400 --> 00:36:04,360
Why does this feel like I'm picking up
a kindergartner after school?

547
00:36:06,360 --> 00:36:07,200
Let's go.

548
00:36:11,440 --> 00:36:14,400
With this sharing session wrapped up,
the project is officially over.

549
00:36:15,120 --> 00:36:16,520
It's completely over.

550
00:36:16,600 --> 00:36:18,920
The professor also gave me
some good news today.

551
00:36:20,200 --> 00:36:21,760
I'm getting a bonus.

552
00:36:22,440 --> 00:36:23,840
Is it from the lab?

553
00:36:23,920 --> 00:36:26,760
He said our results exceeded expectations

554
00:36:26,840 --> 00:36:28,320
and the partners were very pleased.

555
00:36:28,400 --> 00:36:29,480
So they gave us extra money.

556
00:36:30,240 --> 00:36:31,800
Then you should treat yourself.

557
00:36:32,600 --> 00:36:33,440
Of course.

558
00:36:34,120 --> 00:36:36,560
I'm going to use this money to…

559
00:36:36,640 --> 00:36:37,760
Have a feast?

560
00:36:39,640 --> 00:36:41,000
Buy plane tickets back home?

561
00:36:42,560 --> 00:36:45,480
Then buy a gift to reward yourself?

562
00:36:56,200 --> 00:36:57,400
To keep you.

563
00:37:02,800 --> 00:37:04,080
What's wrong?

564
00:37:04,960 --> 00:37:07,120
What… did you just say?

565
00:37:08,120 --> 00:37:11,600
I said I'm going to use the money
to keep you.

566
00:37:12,840 --> 00:37:15,520
I think you have a lot going for you.

567
00:37:15,600 --> 00:37:16,840
You're quite a catch.

568
00:37:17,640 --> 00:37:20,480
You have the looks, you have the physique,

569
00:37:20,560 --> 00:37:21,840
and you're very sweet.

570
00:37:21,920 --> 00:37:23,040
Here's the deal.

571
00:37:23,600 --> 00:37:25,160
I'll take you on a trip.

572
00:37:25,240 --> 00:37:27,320
I'll cover all your expenses.
What do you say?

573
00:37:32,840 --> 00:37:35,800
Does your boyfriend know about this?

574
00:37:41,320 --> 00:37:42,640
How about

575
00:37:42,720 --> 00:37:45,080
we keep it a secret and don't tell him?

576
00:37:45,160 --> 00:37:46,000
Problem solved.

577
00:37:47,760 --> 00:37:49,240
Then let's keep it a secret.

578
00:37:52,640 --> 00:37:55,680
So, does that mean you agree?

579
00:37:57,080 --> 00:37:59,000
Yes, of course I agree.

580
00:37:59,800 --> 00:38:01,000
So where are we going?

581
00:38:01,800 --> 00:38:02,920
You decide.

582
00:38:04,160 --> 00:38:06,040
I'll go wherever you go.

583
00:38:34,440 --> 00:38:37,120
<i>After that day, we took a trip</i>
<i>to Southern France.</i>

584
00:38:38,360 --> 00:38:40,080
<i>The sunshine there</i>
<i>was so generous,</i>

585
00:38:40,160 --> 00:38:42,880
<i>making each day feel a little longer.</i>

586
00:38:44,200 --> 00:38:46,640
<i>So long that</i>
<i>we suddenly realized</i>

587
00:38:46,720 --> 00:38:49,160
<i>we didn't need to</i>
<i>keep ourselves busy</i>

588
00:38:49,240 --> 00:38:51,080
<i>just to fill the time.</i>

589
00:39:10,960 --> 00:39:12,840
<i>We returned to Berlin.</i>

590
00:39:12,920 --> 00:39:14,720
<i>Life didn't change</i>
<i>all that much.</i>

591
00:39:15,360 --> 00:39:17,240
<i>Sometimes,</i>
<i>we'd walk home together.</i>

592
00:39:18,080 --> 00:39:20,360
<i>Those 15 minutes</i>
<i>were the only time all day</i>

593
00:39:21,120 --> 00:39:23,200
<i>when we didn't have</i>
<i>a single thing to worry about.</i>

594
00:39:24,520 --> 00:39:25,360
<i>Most of the time,</i>

595
00:39:25,440 --> 00:39:27,200
<i>we were rushing around</i>
<i>in different places,</i>

596
00:39:27,280 --> 00:39:28,680
<i>fighting our own battles.</i>

597
00:39:29,640 --> 00:39:31,120
<i>Of course,</i>

598
00:39:31,200 --> 00:39:34,320
<i>when classes and experiments</i>
<i>became almost unbearable,</i>

599
00:39:34,400 --> 00:39:37,040
<i>we'd find ways</i>
<i>to lift each other up,</i>

600
00:39:37,120 --> 00:39:38,280
<i>sometimes with a hug,</i>

601
00:39:39,120 --> 00:39:40,680
<i>or…</i>

602
00:39:43,920 --> 00:39:45,520
<i>When we felt anxious,</i>

603
00:39:45,600 --> 00:39:47,760
<i>we'd find ways</i>
<i>to encourage each other.</i>

604
00:39:48,960 --> 00:39:50,640
Well…

605
00:39:52,600 --> 00:39:53,760
You go first.

606
00:40:01,880 --> 00:40:03,720
<i>It was just that</i>
<i>the encouragement we sent out</i>

607
00:40:04,440 --> 00:40:06,200
<i>often found its way back</i>
<i>into our own hands</i>

608
00:40:06,280 --> 00:40:07,640
<i>in mysterious ways.</i>

609
00:40:09,240 --> 00:40:11,960
<i>Sometimes, I'd suddenly feel happy</i>
<i>for no reason at all.</i>

610
00:40:12,040 --> 00:40:13,600
<i>He could always handle it, anyway.</i>

611
00:40:14,720 --> 00:40:17,040
Did you know
Adam came to our school?

612
00:40:17,120 --> 00:40:20,760
We even shared tips
on how to take really great photos!

613
00:40:21,360 --> 00:40:24,920
<i>In autumn, we discovered</i>
<i>a small park near our place.</i>

614
00:40:25,640 --> 00:40:29,360
<i>So on every sunny weekend,</i>
<i>we'd go for a walk there.</i>

615
00:40:30,240 --> 00:40:32,000
<i>Once winter set in in Berlin,</i>

616
00:40:32,080 --> 00:40:34,120
<i>those walks became less frequent.</i>

617
00:40:35,080 --> 00:40:37,640
<i>He's sensitive to the cold,</i>
<i>and I don't like the wind.</i>

618
00:40:38,240 --> 00:40:41,080
<i>So the two of us huddled together</i>
<i>and found a compromise.</i>

619
00:40:42,000 --> 00:40:44,200
<i>Instead of going for walks,</i>
<i>we'd snuggle somewhere cozy.</i>

620
00:40:45,840 --> 00:40:48,360
<i>Just like two little animals</i>
<i>keeping each other warm.</i>

621
00:40:48,440 --> 00:40:50,440
<i>He always says I don't know</i>
<i>how to take care of myself.</i>

622
00:40:51,120 --> 00:40:54,720
<i>But I'm actually pretty good at it.</i>
<i>He's just quicker than I am.</i>

623
00:40:54,800 --> 00:40:57,200
Dad, Mom.
We're just out for a stroll.

624
00:40:57,280 --> 00:40:58,760
Hello!

625
00:40:58,840 --> 00:41:02,880
<i>When spring arrived, we finally</i>
<i>ventured beyond home and campus</i>

626
00:41:02,960 --> 00:41:04,760
<i>to explore nearby cities.</i>

627
00:41:04,840 --> 00:41:08,840
<i>Sometimes he'd video call home</i>
<i>to share the scenery here.</i>

628
00:41:08,920 --> 00:41:10,280
<i>I almost forgot.</i>

629
00:41:10,360 --> 00:41:12,640
<i>We set up a group chat</i>
<i>with his parents.</i>

630
00:41:12,720 --> 00:41:14,080
<i>Gao Xing and Xiaomian are in it too.</i>

631
00:41:15,040 --> 00:41:16,920
<i>Xiaomian pops in now and then,</i>

632
00:41:17,000 --> 00:41:18,960
<i>but as for Gao Xing,</i>

633
00:41:19,760 --> 00:41:21,320
<i>I suspect she's muted the chat.</i>

634
00:41:22,280 --> 00:41:23,200
<i>Oh, right.</i>

635
00:41:23,280 --> 00:41:26,160
<i>I heard his mom has decided</i>
<i>to return to engineering.</i>

636
00:41:27,000 --> 00:41:28,440
<i>We're all so happy for her.</i>

637
00:41:29,280 --> 00:41:31,640
<i>It turns out we're not</i>
<i>the only ones moving forward.</i>

638
00:41:32,240 --> 00:41:35,360
<i>Everyone else is also finding</i>
<i>their own ways to make a fresh start.</i>

639
00:41:36,960 --> 00:41:39,360
<i>After graduation,</i>
<i>we decided to return home.</i>

640
00:41:40,520 --> 00:41:42,160
<i>That summer before we left,</i>

641
00:41:43,320 --> 00:41:44,360
<i>he said</i>

642
00:41:45,080 --> 00:41:47,120
<i>there was something important</i>
<i>he had to do.</i>

643
00:41:52,360 --> 00:41:57,360
CHEN YANZHOU
STARTED SHARING LOCATION

644
00:41:57,440 --> 00:41:59,080
2 PEOPLE ARE
SHARING LOCATIONS

645
00:42:19,800 --> 00:42:21,920
BEACH

646
00:42:27,680 --> 00:42:29,840
CHEN YANZHOU WANTS TO SHARE A VIDEO

647
00:42:33,320 --> 00:42:36,480
<i>Eleonore said that</i>
<i>every time she pressed the shutter,</i>

648
00:42:36,560 --> 00:42:38,560
<i>it felt like pulling the trigger.</i>

649
00:42:38,640 --> 00:42:42,360
<i>As if she was stealing back beautiful</i>
<i>moments from God before they slipped away.</i>

650
00:42:43,320 --> 00:42:45,240
<i>That's why we started taking photos.</i>

651
00:42:45,320 --> 00:42:48,800
<i>Later on, photos alone</i>
<i>weren't enough for me,</i>

652
00:42:48,880 --> 00:42:50,840
<i>so I started recording videos too,</i>

653
00:42:50,920 --> 00:42:54,080
<i>hoping to capture every precious moment.</i>

654
00:42:54,160 --> 00:42:55,120
<i>Taking photos again?</i>

655
00:42:58,320 --> 00:42:59,760
<i>I'm recording a video.</i>

656
00:43:00,280 --> 00:43:01,720
<i>Recording a video?</i>

657
00:43:01,800 --> 00:43:03,600
<i>You seem to really enjoy</i>
<i>taking videos lately.</i>

658
00:43:04,280 --> 00:43:06,160
<i>What are you going to use it for?</i>

659
00:43:07,440 --> 00:43:11,840
<i>If I ever edit a movie and it's released,</i>
<i>you'd better come see it.</i>

660
00:43:15,000 --> 00:43:18,360
<i>Looking back at these recordings</i>
<i>reminds me of when we first met.</i>

661
00:43:19,400 --> 00:43:22,000
<i>You were so different back then</i>
<i>compared to now.</i>

662
00:43:23,280 --> 00:43:24,680
<i>Or maybe</i>

663
00:43:24,760 --> 00:43:26,960
<i>you change with every passing day.</i>

664
00:43:27,640 --> 00:43:29,640
<i>Just like these past few days,</i>

665
00:43:29,720 --> 00:43:31,720
<i>when we've been exploring</i>
<i>so many places together.</i>

666
00:43:50,520 --> 00:43:51,880
<i>We're in Prague.</i>

667
00:43:51,960 --> 00:43:54,000
<i>It's so beautiful! Look!</i>

668
00:43:57,800 --> 00:44:01,160
<i>Sometimes, when you're happy,</i>
<i>you act cute out of nowhere.</i>

669
00:44:02,160 --> 00:44:05,480
<i>Other times, when you're exhausted,</i>
<i>you don't say a word.</i>

670
00:44:06,520 --> 00:44:09,520
<i>Sometimes, when the wind is too strong</i>
<i>and messes up your hair,</i>

671
00:44:09,600 --> 00:44:11,800
<i>I get to see you</i>
<i>letting out that little sigh.</i>

672
00:44:12,800 --> 00:44:16,640
<i>I've realized that I love</i>
<i>every side of you.</i>

673
00:44:18,160 --> 00:44:19,000
<i>Zheng Yu.</i>

674
00:44:20,640 --> 00:44:21,480
<i>Zheng Yu.</i>

675
00:44:22,160 --> 00:44:23,320
<i>Zheng Yu!</i>

676
00:44:24,120 --> 00:44:25,360
<i>Zheng Yu!</i>

677
00:44:26,480 --> 00:44:27,680
<i>Zheng Yu.</i>

678
00:44:30,760 --> 00:44:31,600
Zheng Yu.

679
00:44:45,680 --> 00:44:46,600
I think

680
00:44:47,360 --> 00:44:49,680
if we are going to
be together for a long time,

681
00:44:49,760 --> 00:44:51,120
for ten years,

682
00:44:51,200 --> 00:44:52,680
twenty years,

683
00:44:52,760 --> 00:44:53,880
or fifty years,

684
00:44:55,440 --> 00:44:57,000
so many more changes

685
00:44:57,080 --> 00:44:58,920
will happen to us along the way.

686
00:45:00,200 --> 00:45:01,840
<i>I want to know</i>
<i>how the person you are today</i>

687
00:45:01,920 --> 00:45:03,920
<i>is different from the person</i>
<i>you were yesterday.</i>

688
00:45:04,640 --> 00:45:06,760
<i>I want to know what will make you cry</i>

689
00:45:06,840 --> 00:45:08,320
<i>when you're 30,</i>

690
00:45:09,280 --> 00:45:12,320
<i>and what will make you laugh</i>
<i>when you're 40.</i>

691
00:45:14,160 --> 00:45:18,000
<i>I want to know if, when you grow old,</i>
<i>you'll still be just like you are now,</i>

692
00:45:18,600 --> 00:45:22,240
<i>challenging me to see who's better,</i>

693
00:45:22,320 --> 00:45:26,520
<i>or coming up with</i>
<i>more silly things for us to do.</i>

694
00:45:28,640 --> 00:45:29,880
<i>Perhaps</i>

695
00:45:31,080 --> 00:45:33,720
you'll show many more sides
of yourself over the years.

696
00:45:33,800 --> 00:45:34,960
But I think

697
00:45:35,760 --> 00:45:37,920
I will stay forever curious about you.

698
00:45:39,960 --> 00:45:42,480
I'll never make you feel like
I know everything about you.

699
00:45:44,880 --> 00:45:48,120
I want to be the first
to notice every change in you,

700
00:45:48,720 --> 00:45:50,280
then smile and ask,

701
00:45:51,320 --> 00:45:53,160
"What happened today?"

702
00:45:59,600 --> 00:46:00,960
So…

703
00:46:13,280 --> 00:46:14,280
Zheng Yu.

704
00:46:14,960 --> 00:46:16,560
Will you marry me?

705
00:46:17,440 --> 00:46:21,000
Will you let me become
your one and only legal husband?

706
00:46:26,840 --> 00:46:28,000
I…

707
00:46:28,080 --> 00:46:29,160
I will!

708
00:47:43,680 --> 00:47:45,400
Are we taking all of this
back home?

709
00:47:45,480 --> 00:47:47,160
Or should we leave it
with Marco for now

710
00:47:47,240 --> 00:47:48,680
and have him
ship it to us later?

711
00:47:51,280 --> 00:47:52,480
What are you doing?

712
00:47:53,320 --> 00:47:55,360
Gao Xing wants to make
a video for our wedding.

713
00:47:55,960 --> 00:47:58,760
She said it would be
her way of congratulating us,

714
00:47:58,840 --> 00:48:01,640
and that it also counts
as her class assignment too.

715
00:48:01,720 --> 00:48:02,920
She asked me to

716
00:48:03,000 --> 00:48:03,920
record more footage.

717
00:48:04,000 --> 00:48:05,840
We don't actually have
to hold this camera up

718
00:48:05,920 --> 00:48:07,760
all the way from Berlin to Qingyi, do we?

719
00:48:08,600 --> 00:48:10,880
That's exactly what she told me to do.

720
00:48:12,920 --> 00:48:14,520
Aren't we spoiling her a bit too much?

721
00:48:16,720 --> 00:48:18,480
It's a 12-hour flight back home.

722
00:48:18,560 --> 00:48:20,240
I want some private time
for just the two of us.

723
00:48:21,560 --> 00:48:23,080
Okay, no more filming then!

724
00:48:27,040 --> 00:48:28,080
We're on strike!

725
00:48:28,160 --> 00:48:29,120
On strike!

726
00:48:33,760 --> 00:48:34,840
Well…

727
00:48:34,920 --> 00:48:37,240
A teacher for a day
is a father for a lifetime.

728
00:48:37,320 --> 00:48:38,440
In this case, cousin-in-law!

729
00:48:39,080 --> 00:48:40,360
Be serious.

730
00:48:40,440 --> 00:48:41,720
This is for our wedding video.

731
00:48:42,440 --> 00:48:43,320
Let's do it again.

732
00:48:46,200 --> 00:48:49,000
Our new journey is about to begin.

733
00:48:50,600 --> 00:48:51,480
Let's go!

734
00:49:01,880 --> 00:49:02,960
Bye!

735
00:49:05,720 --> 00:49:06,680
Hey.

736
00:49:08,560 --> 00:49:11,520
THIS DRAMA IS FOR EVERYONE WHO HAS EVER
FELT THAT LIFE WAS UNBEARABLE AT NIGHT.

737
00:49:11,600 --> 00:49:14,320
PERHAPS YOU'RE WEATHERING THE RAIN,
OR WALKING ALONE THROUGH DARKNESS.

738
00:49:14,400 --> 00:49:16,920
BUT ONE DAY, YOU'LL REALIZE
YOU'RE STRONGER THAN YOU EVER IMAGINED.

739
00:49:17,000 --> 00:49:19,160
MAY WE ALL FIND THE STRENGTH
TO WEATHER LIFE'S HARDSHIPS.

740
00:49:19,240 --> 00:49:21,440
THEN, TOGETHER, WALK TOWARDS
A TOMORROW WITHOUT STORMS.

741
00:49:24,360 --> 00:49:26,360
Chen Yanzhou, a quick interview.

742
00:49:26,440 --> 00:49:28,960
Where would you ideally
want to take our wedding photos?

743
00:49:30,360 --> 00:49:31,680
The location doesn't matter.

744
00:49:31,760 --> 00:49:33,720
It could be on a street, by the sea,

745
00:49:33,800 --> 00:49:35,080
or even at home.

746
00:49:36,120 --> 00:49:39,200
I think as long as we're together,
the photos will be beautiful.

747
00:49:39,800 --> 00:49:40,920
I feel the same way.

748
00:50:10,800 --> 00:50:11,800
You look beautiful.

749
00:50:12,720 --> 00:50:13,800
You look handsome too.

750
00:51:02,560 --> 00:51:05,080
<i>It's a sunset.</i>

751
00:51:05,160 --> 00:51:06,400
<i>A sunset.</i>

752
00:51:26,880 --> 00:51:30,480
THEIR STORY HAS COME TO AN END,
BUT YOUR LIFE GOES ON.

753
00:51:30,560 --> 00:51:34,280
IF YOU EVER ENCOUNTER A SUN-SHOWER AGAIN,
WE HOPE IT REMINDS YOU OF THIS DRAMA.

754
00:51:34,360 --> 00:51:38,640
REMEMBER ZHENG YU AND CHEN YANZHOU,
AND ALL THOSE LITTLE, VIVID MOMENTS.

